Book of Proof — Richard Hammack (@math-source-proof: 0, is #book) { r_027C6E588EEF719F2C13655FF8
Richard Hammack, Book of Proof, third edition, revision 3.4. English. Copyright 2018; the author's page dates revision 3.4 to 5 February 2025.

[Author's edition page](https://richardhammack.github.io/BookOfProof/) · [Authorized PDF](https://richardhammack.github.io/BookOfProof/Main.pdf).

For this foundation block, read chapters 1–2 and chapter 4. Work exercises using the arithmetic, set and logical concepts introduced here. Record examples requiring unfamiliar trigonometry or calculus for the later foundation pass instead of guessing their notation. Later formation must complete those deferred exercises and the remaining proof methods and structures; these selections do not complete the book.

The author supplies free access under CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. This source is linked, not copied or adapted; no PDF is bundled. Preserve the author, edition and actual notice when consulting or sharing it.

Inspection on 31 October 2026: author page, PDF edition/license page, contents, and selected opening passages of sections 2.7, 2.10 and 4.3. Those passages support the reading selection; the assigned chapters and all their exercises were not fully audited. Trail explanations and exercises are independently written.

**Seventh mathematics-core source inspection — 1 November 2026:** the author page and PDF confirm third edition/revision 3.4, 5 February 2025 revision notice and CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. Actual selected passages from counting/multisets and section 3.9, induction in 10.1, and equivalence classes/partitions in 11.3–11.4 were inspected. The common study independently reconstructs the finite sum-to-nine claim of Example 3.24 and checks all 210 six-member subsets of the stated ten-element domain. Complete chapters 1, 3, 8, 10–12 progressively with exercises as their preparation is established; full chapters and exercise sets were not audited or performed by this bounded inspection. Existing assignments remain. All source media stay external and the token construction/programs are original.

